                    },
                    "message": "Done, thanks for review."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Item/Accelerator.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "This is not specific to accelerators, is it?\n\nMin/Max power consumption applies to many things like\n\n- Dimm\n- Drive\n- Baseboard\n- Fan\n- Cpu\n- Chassis\n\nDid you consider to make this an independent interface?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Item/Accelerator.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Eric Liu",
                        "email": "liuer@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "liuer-sys"
                    },
                    "message": "Agreed. Moved MinPowerWatts/MaxPowerWatts out of Item.Accelerator into a new cross-cutting decorator, Inventory.Decorator.PowerBounds, that any inventory item (chassis, processor, accelerator, ...) can implement."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Item/Accelerator.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 32,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "Can the same thing be achieved with the existing `Control.Power.Cap` or `Control.Power.CapLimits` interface?"
                }
            ],
